From f575f4c8b7431e2ba35e4baf9521b8a24cfe20b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: George Whewell <georgerw@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 14:50:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: coda: add SG2002 Coda980 H.264 encoder

The SG2002 integrates a Chips&Media Coda980 H.264 encoder. The core
speaks the Coda9 register command ABI, but it is not an i.MX Coda: the
firmware expects its code, temporary, and parameter slices inside one
768 KiB DMA common arena, its version word reports a customer product
code, and the SoC's simple-reset controller cannot pulse the H.264
reset line.

Add the SG2002 Coda980 platform data and wire it through the driver:
a single H.264 encoder video device, the common-arena layout with its
CODE/TEMP/PARA offsets, NV21-to-NV12 input staging through a coherent
buffer, and the firmware boot sequence. The register recipe and buffer
layout come from the vendor SG2002 kernel source and the observed
behaviour of the factory 3.0.1 firmware; no vendor code is reused.

Tested on the SG2002 NanoKVM with 1080p NV21 input.

Signed-off-by: George Whewell <georgerw@gmail.com>
